el coronavirus we're  all entitled to be wrong as experts as  doctors because medicine is an imperfect  science I've said in other videos how  medicine is as much art as it is science  because two doctors can look at the same  situation and have different  interpretations of it I think where he  went wrong was he forgot somewhat that  medicine carries within itself a level  of humility we have to approach it with  a level of humility to me if dr. drew  came out and said something like  look I think in my own expert opinion  that this novel coronavirus won't be as  bad as the media is making it seem but  we'll keep looking at the information I  think that would have been a reasonable  statement to make even though he was  wrong at the end all of this really  serves as a stark reminder that expert  opinion is and should always be  considered the lowest form of evidence  when we talk about levels of evidence we  look at expert opinion basically when a  doctor thinks is right then we move up  to a case series observational studies  then the gold standard randomized  controlled studies then you even have  one up on that where you have a meta  analyses which is many randomized  controlled studies I am pleased to  report though that dr. Jew did issue  this apology my early comments about  equating coronavirus with influenza were  wrong they were incorrect that was part  of a chorus that was saying that and we  were wrong and I want to apologize for  that  interestingly the verb that we use for  medicine is practicing we practice  medicine because we're all bound to make  a mistake especially with how imperfect  our knowledge is for continuously  evolving it and doing better and trying  harder all in all I hope to see dr. drew  bounce back from this incident I know  millions of people look to dr. drew for  medical advice and he brings a really  unique vantage point to medical media  being that he's dually board-certified  in addiction and internal medicine with  a huge focus on mental health I've heard  that dr. Drew's media team has been  issuing copyright takedown notices for  people using the clips that I just used  I really hope they don't come after us  as this is a good learning opportunity  next up we have another popular medical  media figure dr. oz you received some  serious backlash on Twitter for comments  he made on Fox News take a look the  panic attack is devastating and it is a  physical problem it's not just in your  head you're a whole body they have the  rapid palpitations the sweating that  they're feeling think the world is  closing in around you and these symptoms  can cause all kinds of detrimental  effect which is why I think a lot of  doctors now are feeling that the worry  in the panic about coronavirus is gonna  be worse than the actual coronavirus for  them the majority of criticism from  Twitter came from the fact that they  felt dr. oz was misrepresenting the  views of doctors on the  lines who are legitimately more  concerned about coronavirus than they  anxiety that can potentially come from  it I actually happen to agree with  Twitter on this one I have a lot of  doctor friends who are on the front  lines a great example would be dr.  Donald Pettit who was actually in my  hundred doctors video he's an ER  resident  who happens to be working in the ICU  right now he tells me about the  equipment shortages the ICU and  ventilator use that's gone up  tremendously over the last few weeks and  it's scary to him I mean he's on the  front lines potentially getting himself  sick bringing the virus home to his  family he has a newborn baby at home so  I actually went ahead and texted dr. oz  I mentioned the negative criticism he  was getting my thoughts on the subject  and I'm happy to report he was quite  welcoming of that and he said that in  the following interviews he was gonna  make a change in the way he spoke about  this and correct his previous statements  I do live television quite often and I  know how easy it is to have one thing in  your mind and then speak something that  comes out somewhat different so I was  appreciative the fact that dr. oz was  open to this type of feedback and was  willing to change his statements in the  future I think that's how we as doctors  really have to function in order to be  more effective communicators and better  at relaying crucial medical information  to the general public  up next we have quite the polarizing  figure in dr. Joseph Mercola  dr. Joseph Mercola is a practicing  physician he takes a naturopathic  approach to how he treats his patients  he's quite popular online he's actually  found himself in hot water quite a few  times with the FDA for making  unsubstantiated claims about products  that he sells on his website and I  haven't really found any claims that I  was interested in debunking until I saw  a few recent tweets that caught my  attention the first tweet read us such  while unproven one current theory is  that electromagnetic field radiation and  the addition of 5g in particular could  be having an impact on the Cova 19:00  pandemic this is actually a very common  conspiracy theory that's being put out  there on social media forums on reddit  what-have-you here's the problem no  evidence exists to support this theory  let me talk about briefly how we create  theories in science and then how we go  about testing them first and foremost  you have  to have an idea with a plausible  mechanism of how that idea comes to be  for example if you wanted to create  antibiotics before there are antibiotics  you have to think to yourself well this  antibiotic can work in this method to  kill this bacteria thereby eliminating  it from the system you go ahead you  tried it lab models animal models human  models and you work your way out here  there is no plausible mechanism for how  EMF waves or 5g makes people have worse  cases of the novel coronavirus that's  why I wish this tweet ended when he said  while unproven because while it's  unproven we can make any random  correlative statement the fact that  February had an extra day this year  could be a reason why Cova 19 is  affecting us so seriously  you can literally substitute that with  anything and that goes to speak to the  power of the difference between  correlation and causation  remember correlation two things  happening simultaneously 5g and  coronavirus causation is when something  directly causes that thing to happen the  next tweet which i think is the more  problematic of the two reads of such  nebulous hydrogen peroxide therapy is an  inexpensive and simple way to treat most  viral respiratory illnesses all you need  is a nebulizer with a face mask that  covers your mouth and nose and common  household hydrogen peroxide available at  most grocery stores and pharmacies now  there's a few things to unpack here  first and foremost the cdc and fda  clearly state that there exists no  proven methods to treat or prevent kovat  19 and to me when a doctor believes  their own expert opinion outweighs those  of major medical organizations like the  cdc and fda  without substantial evidence you're  crossing a line next let's talk about  the dangers of inhaled hydrogen peroxide  straight from the cdc website hydrogen  peroxide is not absorbed by the skin  but can cause systemic toxicity when  inhaled or ingested I have to read this  next whole segment cause of how serious  is vapours missed or aerosols of  hydrogen peroxide can cause upper airway  irritation inflammation of the nose  hoarseness shortness of breath and a  sensation of burning or tightness in the  chest exposure to high concentrations  can result in severe mucosal congestion  of the trachea and  and delayed accumulation of fluid in the  lungs children may be more vulnerable to  corrosive agents than adults because of  the relatively smaller diameter of their  Airways dr. Mercola  in his own YouTube video actually states  that you should not use common household  